usal chain with the existing drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions suppression (run_differs.py:279) that already discards all (outbound, update)/field_drift before apply/tally — show, with measured evidence, that the ~516 mutations actually reach applier.py:639-640 despite that drop (or restate the true problem being solved).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["run_differs.py:279 `mutations = drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions(mutations)` runs before `ctx.mutations = mutations` at run_differs.py:292","reconcile_helpers.py:117 drop-list entry `(\"outbound\", \"update\", \"field_drift\")` — exactly what _compute_mutations_emit_both emits (differ.py:601-614 reason='field_drift')","reconcile_helpers.py:142-144: 'The snapshot route drops this phantom before apply'","Plan Why: 'Each inert mutation still drives one per-mutation loop iteration in the batch apply path (applier.py:639-640) ... So ~516 extra git invocations per pass'"],"finding":"The plan's causal chain (branch-3 inert mutations reach the batch apply path at applier.py:639-640 and drive ~516 git rev-parse calls / outcome records / inflated mutation_count) contradicts an existing suppression at the very call site the plan targets: run_differs.py:279 calls drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions immediately after compute_mutations, which drops the ENTIRE (outbound, update)/field_drift class before ctx.mutations is set (run_differs.py:292) and before apply. Its docstring says 'The snapshot route drops this phantom before apply.'","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd8e42fc1441400e8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Why' section; run_differs.py:269-292; reconcile_helpers.py:115-196","norm_id":"n6263ad957b4a10b9","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Key-set prev over a real corpus at the run_differs call site — the ~516 field_drift mutations are already discarded before tally/apply"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Compare the chosen compute_mutations-flag approach against the existing drop-list locus (reconcile_helpers.py:_SNAPSHOT_DIFFER_LOCAL_STATE_EMISSIONS) and justify why upstream per-key skipping beats broadening/relocating the existing downstream drop, or adopt the existing mechanism; add reconcile_helpers.py to Files if it must change.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Files list: differ.py, _field_contract.py, dispatch_apply_phases.py, run_differs.py, tests — no reconcile_helpers.py","reconcile_helpers.py:171-173: 'differ.compute_mutations itself is deliberately NOT modified — its documented local-vs-jira contract stays intact ... the suppression lives at the one call site that does not' — the plan proposes the opposite (modify compute_mutations)","Plan Approach: 'Add an explicit opt-in flag to compute_mutations ... skips branch-3 update emission for keys whose local-side value is empty'"],"finding":"The plan's approach (add an opt-in flag to compute_mutations so branch-3 skips empty-local keys) is narrower than and overlaps an existing downstream mechanism (the _SNAPSHOT_DIFFER_LOCAL_STATE_EMISSIONS drop-list) that already removes the whole field_drift class at the same call site. The plan neither mentions this helper nor selects between the two loci, and reconcile_helpers.py is absent from the Files list.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbd0bb99bb2ea63c0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Approach' and 'Files' sections; reconcile_helpers.py:115-196","norm_id":"n90a3a5de64a532bc","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Non-empty field_drift from remote-prev vs remote-curr at run_differs: the plan's flag leaves it emitted (only empty-local skipped), so it still relies on the existing drop-list to remove it — two overlapping suppressions with different scopes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"high","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly whether A4-2 removes/bypasses reconcile_helpers.drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions (which already drops all (outbound,update,field_drift) branch-3 mutations at the sole production caller run_differs.py:269-279); if it does not, justify why a NEW compute_mutations flag + emit-time skip is needed rather than reusing/relying on that existing suppression.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile_helpers.py:115-120: _SNAPSHOT_DIFFER_LOCAL_STATE_EMISSIONS includes ('outbound','update','field_drift')","reconcile_helpers.py:123-196: drops matching mutations with provenance source=='differ' at the run_differs call site","run_differs.py:269 then 279: compute_mutations(...) output is immediately reassigned via drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions(mutations)","differ.py:610-615: branch-3 emits reason='field_drift', source='differ' — exactly the dropped signature","grep: compute_mutations( has exactly ONE production caller (run_differs.py:269); all others are tests + docs/experiments corpus script"],"finding":"The plan adds a new opt-in flag to compute_mutations to skip branch-3 (outbound,update,field_drift) emission, but the sole production caller (run_differs.py:269) already passes compute_mutations' output through reconcile_helpers.drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions (run_differs.py:279), which unconditionally drops every ('outbound','update','field_drift') differ emission before apply. As written, the new flag rebuilds suppression that already exists at the same call site (NIH / redundant config surface), unless A4-2 removes that existing drop — which the plan does not state.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc306a5872fef5d11","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section; Files/Scope line ('Depends on A4-2')","norm_id":"nc1ffc896426cc945","priority":0.9,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Production LIVE pass over a key-set prev where the existing drop already removes the ~516 field_drift mutations before apply","A reviewer/maintainer later finds two overlapping suppression mechanisms for the same mutation signature"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"high","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile AC2's 'dedicated outbound sub-calls before scalar filtering' with differ.py: _compute_mutations_emit_both treats parent/reporter as ordinary scalars (no sub-calls); restate the negative control in terms of the actual field-by-field diff path or clarify which differ (differ.py vs outbound_differ.py) the control targets.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.035,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Grep of differ.py for 'reporter' returns (no matches); 'parent' matches are only Path(__file__).parent and a comment — no parent/reporter special-casing.","differ.py:578-597 _compute_mutations_emit_both iterates `set(local_fields) | set(jira_fields)`, applies EXCLUDED_FIELDS + label-internal skip + conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES, then `changed[field] = local_val` for any other differing scalar — parent/reporter are undistinguished.","The dedicated parent handling (local_parents map, non-epic suppression) is in outbound_differ.py:497-554, which is invoked separately in run_differs (_run_differs_outbound), not by compute_mutations."],"finding":"AC2 asserts parent-only and reporter-only branch-3 changes 'route through dedicated outbound sub-calls before scalar filtering', but differ.py's _compute_mutations_emit_both (the branch-3 the plan modifies) treats every field, including parent and reporter, as an ordinary scalar in a plain field-by-field diff loop with no dedicated sub-calls. The 'dedicated outbound sub-calls' mechanism lives in outbound_differ.py, a separate differ that compute_mutations never invokes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f43b9d3717fa59531","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC2), 'route through dedicated outbound sub-calls before scalar filtering'","norm_id":"nc7c32b319427e011","priority":0.765,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An author writes the AC2 negative-control unit test against compute_mutations expecting a parent-only or reporter-only change to traverse 'dedicated outbound sub-calls'; no such path exists in differ.py, so the test's premise is wrong even though a parent-only diff DOES still emit via the ordinary scalar path."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Rephrase AC2 to: 'parent-only and reporter-only changes still emit a branch-3 outbound update via the ordinary scalar field-by-field diff (they are non-empty local values), and are NOT suppressed by the new empty-local opt-in'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cit